To find $A$ and $B$, we take the following equation and multiply both sides by the common denominator:

$\begin{align}
\displaystyle\dfrac{4x-11}{(2x-1)(x+4)}&=\dfrac{A}{2x-1}+\dfrac{B}{x+4}
\\\\
\displaystyle {4x-11}&={A(x+4)}+{B(2x-1)}
\end{align}$

Substituting $x=\dfrac12$, we get $\blueD{A=-2}$.

Substituting $x=-4$, we get $\maroonD{B=3}$.
